  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;li&gt;Rejected Plans&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;AA-A2130.02_S_P-2002&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;AA-A2130.02_S_p-4000&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;AA-A2130.02_S_P-3001&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;AA-A2130.02_S_P-3000&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;AA-A2130.02_S_P-2003&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;AA-A2130.02_S_P-2001&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;AA-A2130.02_S_P-2000&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;AA-A2130.02_S_P-0001&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;AA-A2130.02_S_P-0000 &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;AA-A2130.02_S_e-4001&lt;/li&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed ground floor bedroom window would result in an unacceptable loss of privacy owing to its overlooking relationship with the first floor flat at no. 136 Coombe Lane, resulting in a substandard living environment for future occupiers, contrary to London Plan (2021) policy D6 (Housing quality and standards) and Merton Local Plan (2024) policy D12.3 (Ensuring high quality design for all developments).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed dwelling would introduce a substantial and incongruous form of backland/garden development into an area presently characterised by open, undeveloped rear garden land, together with an intensification of activity uncharacteristic of its garden setting, resulting in harm to the visual amenity, character and appearance of the site and its surroundings, contrary to National Decision Making Policy DP3 (Key principles for well-designed places) of the National Planning Policy Framework 2026, London Plan (2021) policy D4 (Delivering good design), and Merton Local Plan (2024) policy D12.3.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;By reason of its scale, siting and the associated intensification of residential activity, noise and artificial lighting, the proposal would result in material harm to the living conditions and privacy of neighbouring occupiers, principally at nos. 134, 136 and 140 Coombe Lane, contrary to National Decision Making Policy P3 (Living conditions and pollution) of the National Planning Policy Framework 2026 and Merton Local Plan (2024) policy D12.3(g).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a completed legal agreement securing a permit-free restriction preventing future occupiers of the development from obtaining on-street parking permits, the proposal fails to demonstrate that the additional parking demand generated would not adversely impact the surrounding highway network, contrary to Merton Local Plan (2024) policies T16.3 (Managing the transport impacts of development) and T16.4 (Parking and Low Emissions Vehicles), and London Plan (2021) policy T6.1 (Residential parking).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
